{"name":"Dove’s Wing","hex":"#f4f2ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigeon, especially one smaller in size and white-colored; a bird (often arbitrarily called either a pigeon or a dove or both) of more than three hundred species of the family Columbidae.","A person favouring conciliation and negotiation rather than conflict."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past of dive","past participle of dive"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dove"},{"term":"wing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An appendage of an animal's (bird, bat, insect) body that enables it to fly.","A fin at the side of a ray or similar fish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To injure slightly (as with a gunshot), especially in the wing or arm.","To fly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing","wikidata":"Q161358"},{"title":"Columbidae","blocks":[{"text":"Columbidae is a bird family consisting of doves and pigeons. It is the only family in the order Columbiformes. These are stout-bodied birds with small heads, relatively short necks and slender bills that in some species feature fleshy ceres. They feed largely on plant matter, feeding on seeds (granivory), fruit (frugivory), and foliage (folivory)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg/330px-Treron_vernans_male_-_Kent_Ridge_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbidae","wikidata":"Q10856"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/500px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/1280px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/500px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Condensation in the low-pressure region over the wing of an Airbus A340, passing through humid air","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACloud_over_A340_wing.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg/500px-Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg/1280px-Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg/500px-Bmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The wing of a landing BMI Airbus A319-100. The slats at its leading edge and the flaps at its trailing edge are extended.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABmi_a319-100_g-dbca_closeup_arp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/PSM_V19_D181_Various_seeds_of_trees.jpg/1